#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SE1157 expect=violation domain=CM
#note "CMRSTIND variable not present at all but CMRSTMOD is populated -> fires via the bare empty(--RSTIND) leaf, TRUE on every row of the absent column (absent = all-missing, EC-43). (Plan B phase 4d' deleted the redundant `or not var_exists(--RSTIND)` disjunct this note used to name; the verdict is unchanged.) RE-POINTED TO expect=skipped BY PLAN-retire-corpus-transforms PHASE 4 AND REVERTED 2026-08-26: that hoist's stated warrant was the Fix #330 remedy 'a presence rule reports the absence once', and NO presence rule for --RSTIND exists anywhere in the corpus -- so the SKIP left the absence entirely unreported. --RSTIND is back out of Requirements.Variables.All."
#library standard=sendig version=ar-1-0
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 CMSEQ=1
dataset CM class=INTERVENTIONS label="Concomitant Medications"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col CMSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col CMRSTMOD type=Char label="Restraint Mode"
---
S1 | CM | 001 | 1 | SLING
S1 | CM | 001 | 2 |
